viewerT -- SEQ 686 (the show dispatch, stroke 1: the viewer). show opens the PDF it wrote to its output path when viewer (pROPERTIEs)
is 1 and the shell's INCANT_NOVIEW is not set; it never opens another path. This fixture never writes IncantForms/PDF/output.pdf:
for VT-1 and VT-2 it points showPath, the output path, at test.pdf; for VT-3 it puts showPath back and shows a form whose own path
is test.pdf. formsPop runs it with INCANT_NOVIEW=1, as every script of Clod's does.
    VT-1  viewer = 0: "=== show viewer off ===", no open attempted.
    VT-2  viewer = 1 but INCANT_NOVIEW set: viewer off, no open attempted.
    VT-3  the path is not the output path: no viewer line of any kind.
    viewer on with nothing set opens the system's default viewer in the background: checked by Tony's eye, not here.
